      "finding_id": "HR-002",
      "packet_id": "HR-002",
      "parent_finding_id": "HR-002",
      "assessment": "needs_more_evidence",
      "reason": "Reachability: not established from `src/Api/Webhooks/Handlers/WebhookHandler.php:19`; that method only hooks `init_hooks`, while the AJAX surface in this packet is registered in `src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php:25-29`, and the packet does not prove `AddFormNotice::init()` runs. Authorization: the route is authenticated-only because only `wp_ajax_...` is registered at `src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php:28`, and `check_ajax_referer()` gates the handler at `src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php:44`, although no capability check follows. Dataflow: `$_POST['choice']` reaches the `dismiss` transient write through `src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php:45-59` when a valid nonce is present. Impact: the demonstrated effect is a shared notice-dismiss transient checked by `src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php:117-129`; the `success` branch only returns a fixed admin URL at `src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php:63-67`, so the packet overstates this as subscriber privilege escalation. Missing evidence: runtime registration of `AddFormNotice::init()` and concrete proof that a low-privilege role can obtain the localized nonce on a whitelisted screen.",
      "required_changes": [
        "Correct the entry point and anchor set: do not cite `src/Api/Webhooks/Handlers/WebhookHandler.php:19` for this AJAX finding; the in-packet route registration is `src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php:25-29`.",
        "Correct `auth_required` from `unknown`/implicit subscriber reachability to authenticated-only unless separate evidence shows nonce exposure beyond authenticated admin-screen users.",
        "Downgrade the impact description from subscriber privilege escalation to a nonce-gated shared notice-dismiss/UI-state change unless low-privilege nonce acquisition and boundary crossing are proven.",
        "Keep the missing capability-check observation conditional on proof that `AddFormNotice::init()` is actually invoked at runtime."
      ],
      "counter_evidence": [
        {
          "type": "unreachable",
          "file": "src/Api/Webhooks/Handlers/WebhookHandler.php",
          "line": 19,
          "detail": "This cited entry point only registers `$this->init_hooks()` on the global `init` hook; the packet shows no in-scope call edge from `WebhookHandler` to `AddFormNotice::handle_ajax_action()`."
        },
        {
          "type": "guard",
          "file": "src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php",
          "line": 28,
          "detail": "The handler is registered only on `wp_ajax_hostinger_reach_add_form_notice_action`; there is no `wp_ajax_nopriv_...` route in scope, so unauthenticated reachability is refuted and the auth boundary is narrower than claimed."
        },
        {
          "type": "guard",
          "file": "src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php",
          "line": 44,
          "detail": "A valid action nonce is required before the branch executes, so exploitability depends on proving nonce delivery to the claimed low-privilege actor."
        },
        {
          "type": "scope",
          "file": "src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php",
          "line": 103,
          "detail": "`should_render()` restricts notice rendering and asset delivery to specific admin screens and plugin state (`dashboard`, `pages`, `posts`, `edit-page`, `edit-post`, connected, not dismissed, no forms), so nonce exposure is conditional rather than universal."
        },
        {
          "type": "impact",
          "file": "src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php",
          "line": 59,
          "detail": "The `dismiss` branch only writes the shared `hostinger_reach_add_form_notice_dismissed` transient for one week; this is a notice/UI-state change, not a capability or settings change."
        },
        {
          "type": "impact",
          "file": "src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php",
          "line": 66,
          "detail": "The `success` branch only returns a hardcoded admin URL string and does not modify options, webhook configuration, or user privileges."
        }
      ],
      "missing_evidence": [
        "A concrete plugin file:line showing `AddFormNotice::init()` is invoked during normal plugin bootstrap; the packet only shows the method body that would register the AJAX action.",
        "Concrete evidence that a Subscriber/Customer or equivalent low-privilege principal can receive the localized nonce created at `src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php:155` despite the `should_render()` gating at `src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php:100-121`.",
        "A concrete path or PoC showing that the transient write at `src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php:59` crosses a meaningful security boundary beyond hiding the notice."
      ],
      "expansion_attempts": [],
      "suggested_field_corrections": {
        "auth_required": "authenticated",
        "entry_point_anchor": "src/Admin/Notices/AddFormNotice.php:28",
        "vuln_type": "Authenticated AJAX handler missing explicit capability check for shared notice-dismiss action",
        "claimed_impact": "Nonce-gated shared admin-notice dismissal/UI-state change; subscriber/customer privilege escalation not demonstrated",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    }
  ]
